      "published_at_source": "RETAINED_MAIN_REPORT_KNOWN_AT_NOT_PUBLICATION_CLOCK",
      "canonical_content_text": "Base case (56%): gold is lower in 24 hours after losing a floor that had held five times since 16 November. Mechanism: trend selling and stops below 3832.288 in a market down 17.5% over 60 sessions; the driver of the first push at 00:00 UTC is not identified. Priced: about 25 below the 23:45 UTC close at the capture bid of 3823.598, below the 20-session range low of 3852.401. Positioning: not observed. Driver: structure and trend; an unverified U.S. strike lead that would normally lift gold drew no bid, and crude did not move either. Confirmations: the 00:15 M15 close of 3830.973 below 3832.288 and a fresh low for the 60 daily bars shown. Invalidation: a completed H1 bar closing above 3858.19. Main alternative (44%): the drop is a stop run and gold is back above 3832.288 within the session.",
